# Measured, not written by hand: `TM_CORPUS_BLESS=1 cargo test --test corpus`.
#
# kind \t name \t outcome \t detail
#
# `corpus_round_trip` asserts only that every row recorded `ok` is still
# `ok`.  A row that starts passing is reported, not failed: the grammar is
# being extended on other branches and this number may only rise.  The
# `detail` column is a note, not an assertion.
#
# `reject` is the kernel refusing to load the file at all.  It is never
# "the file changed": a document the kernel accepts and hands back with
# different bytes is `differs`, and `no_file_is_silently_rewritten` fails
# on it unconditionally, with no baseline.
